  "goodToKnow": "Herrschend means ruling or prevailing: die herrschende Partei, die herrschenden Verhältnisse (prevailing conditions). In German law, die herrschende Meinung (abbreviated h. M.) is the prevailing view among courts and scholars, a phrase every law student learns. The verb herrschen means to rule or to prevail: Es herrscht Chaos (chaos reigns). Die Herrschaft is rule or reign, and der Herrscher a ruler."
